INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - DAY

ZAYAN (9) stands frozen before a glass trophy case. He is a South Asian boy with tight dark curls. He wears a bright red hoodie with a frayed left cuff and scuffed white trainers.

He is never fully still. His feet tap a silent, rapid rhythm.

Inside the glass case sits a shiny plastic action figure: the NEBULA-9 GOLDEN COMMANDER. It has chrome armor and a tiny glowing laser sword.

Zayan wants that action figure. He wants it more than anything in the world.

He reaches down to his left wrist and pulls a thick blue rubber band. 

*SNAP.*

It hits his wrist. The sharp tap grounds him. He smiles at the toy.

INT. CLASSROOM - DAY

Quiet. Too quiet. 

MR. HENDERSON (40s) stands at the blackboard. He writes with squeaking yellow chalk.

MR. HENDERSON
Number seven. Catastrophe. The storm was a catastrophe.

Zayan sits at his desk. His legs bounce like pistons. He tries to write the word, but his pencil won't move as fast as his thoughts.

His mind is a lightning storm. 

He sees a ladybug crawling on the window pane. He notices the blue ink leaking onto Leo's thumb. He counts thirty-two holes in the ceiling tile above his head. 

Zayan has Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder. His brain does not slow down. It sees every possibility at once.

He writes "CAT" on his paper. Then his pencil slips, tearing the page. He sighs. He pulls his rubber band.

*SNAP.*

Mr. Henderson walks over. He places a hand gently on Zayan's desk.

MR. HENDERSON
(softly)
Zayan. Please try to focus on the paper. We are almost done.

Zayan shrinks into his red hoodie. He pulls the frayed cuff over his hand. He assumes he is in trouble. He always assumes he is in trouble.

ZAYAN
Sorry, Mr. Henderson. My hand got away from me.

Across the aisle, LEO (9) and CHLOE (9) watch. Chloe gives Zayan a sympathetic look. Leo whispers.

LEO
I can't even spell it anyway.

Suddenly, a deep rumble shakes the floorboards. The spelling test papers slide off the desks.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

A loud siren blares. 

*BEEP. BEEP. BEEP.*

On the walls, bright orange lights (#E4572E) flash. Heavy dark slate blue panels (#2E4057) slide down from the ceiling. They block the windows.

INT. CLASSROOM - CONTINUOUS

The classroom door flies open. But the hallway is gone. 

In its place is a towering wall of shifting blue and orange blocks. They slide left and right with a heavy mechanical roar.

MR. HENDERSON
Everyone, stay calm! It is the new security system. It must have malfunctioned!

Mr. Henderson steps out into the doorway to look. 

*WHOOSH.*

A massive slate-blue wall slides shut right in front of him. Mr. Henderson is cut off from the classroom.

LEO
Mr. Henderson!

CHLOE
We're trapped!

The classroom walls begin to slide. The desks are pushed together. 

Zayan stands on his chair. He does not panic. His eyes dart from the ceiling to the floor. While the others see a terrifying mess, Zayan's mind starts tracking the patterns.

ZAYAN
We need to move! Now!

He grabs Chloe and Leo by their sleeves. He pulls them out of the classroom door just as a heavy block seals the room behind them.

INT. SHIFTING MAZE - CONTINUOUS

They stand in a corridor of giant sliding blocks. 

A digital display on the wall flashes: `RE-SHUFFLE IN: 30`.

CHLOE
Where do we go? The whole school is a giant maze!

LEO
We're going to be crushed!

Zayan snaps his rubber band.

*SNAP.*

He closes his eyes for one second. The sound of the sliding walls becomes a rhythm. 

Two blocks slide left. One block slides up. Every thirty seconds, the pattern repeats.

ZAYAN
We aren't going to get crushed. The Principal's Office is at the center of the building. The master override switch is there. And the prize chest!

LEO
Are you thinking about toys right now?

ZAYAN
I can think about three things at once! Follow me!

Zayan darts forward. His scuffed white trainers squeak on the metal floor. 

He does not hesitate. He turns left. He ducks under a descending orange block.

CHLOE
Wait! That's a dead end!

ZAYAN
Only for three more seconds!

Zayan counts down in his head. Three. Two. One.

With a loud hiss, the wall in front of them slides into the floor. A clear path opens.

LEO
How did you know that?

ZAYAN
Because the blue blocks always follow the orange ones! Keep up!

They run through the gap. Behind them, the wall rises again. 

INT. MAZE - INTERSECTION - CONTINUOUS

They reach a massive chamber. Four corridors branch off. Each one has sliding gates that open and close at different speeds.

`RE-SHUFFLE IN: 20`

Chloe looks at the flashing timer. 

CHLOE
Zayan, it's shifting again! Which way?

Zayan's mind races. He sees the speed of each gate. 

Gate one: fast. Gate two: slow. Gate three: closing. Gate four: opening but leading away.

He looks at the floor tiles. The orange tiles form a pathway that aligns only when the timer hits zero.

ZAYAN
We have to wait for the shift.

LEO
Wait? In the middle of a moving maze? We'll get stuck!

ZAYAN
Trust me. If we run now, we get blocked. If we wait, the path opens straight to the office.

Zayan stands in the center. He bounces on his toes. He hates being slowed down. Every muscle in his body wants to run. 

He snaps his rubber band.

*SNAP.*

ZAYAN
(to himself)
Stay still. Just five seconds. Five. Four. Three...

The walls rumble. The ground vibrates.

LEO
Zayan!

ZAYAN
Two. One. Jump!

Zayan grabs their hands and leaps forward. 

As they cross the line, the four walls slide into place behind them with a loud *THUD*. 

A straight, clear corridor lies ahead. At the end of the hall is the glass door of the Principal's Office.

INT. PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

They burst through the door. 

PRINCIPAL HIGGINS (50s) is trapped behind a heavy security partition. He is speaking frantically into a walkie-talkie.

PRINCIPAL HIGGINS
Yes, the whole system is locked down! I can't reach the manual switch!

He looks up and sees the three children.

PRINCIPAL HIGGINS
Kids! How did you get in here? The corridors are completely blocked!

Zayan points to the high wall behind the principal's desk. A red button glows under a plastic cover.

ZAYAN
We tracked the shift pattern! Principal Higgins, you need to hit the red button!

PRINCIPAL HIGGINS
I can't reach it! The safety glass slid down!

Zayan looks around the room. His fast-paced mind spots a narrow opening near the ceiling tiles where the security glass didn't close all the way. 

He looks at the trophy case nearby. The prize chest is open. The Nebula-9 action figure sits on top.

Zayan snaps his rubber band. 

*SNAP.*

He sees the angle. He sees the distance. He sees the solution.

ZAYAN
Leo, give me your ruler! Chloe, I need your notebook!

They hand them over without question.

Zayan slides the notebook into the gap of the safety glass to keep it from sealing shut. He climbs onto the principal's desk.

PRINCIPAL HIGGINS
Young man, that is extremely unsafe!

Zayan uses the long wooden ruler to poke through the gap. He aims for the red button.

He has one shot before the next maze shuffle locks the glass permanently.

His hand is steady. His mind is perfectly clear.

*CLICK.*

He presses the button.

With a loud hiss of releasing air, the heavy slate-blue panels rise. The orange lights stop flashing. 

The walls slide back into the ceilings. The school hallway returns to normal.

Mr. Henderson runs down the hallway, gasping for breath.

MR. HENDERSON
Zayan! Leo! Chloe! Are you alright?

Zayan steps down from the desk. He suddenly feels very small. He pulls his red hood over his curls. He assumes he is in trouble.

ZAYAN
I'm sorry I climbed on the desk, Principal Higgins. And I'm sorry we ran away, Mr. Henderson.

Principal Higgins stares at the manual override switch, then at Zayan.

PRINCIPAL HIGGINS
In trouble? My boy, you just saved the entire school from a weekend lockdown!

Leo steps forward, grinning widely.

LEO
He was like a super-computer! He saw the walls moving and just knew where to go!

CHLOE
He didn't even hesitate. Your brain is amazing, Zayan!

Zayan looks at his classmates. They aren't laughing. They aren't annoyed that he was moving too fast. They are looking at him with genuine admiration.

Mr. Henderson smiles warmly and walks over to the open prize chest.

MR. HENDERSON
I believe someone earned a very special prize today.

Mr. Henderson picks up the Nebula-9 Golden Commander action figure and hands it to Zayan.

Zayan takes the toy. It is cold, heavy, and perfect. He beams.

ZAYAN
Thank you, Mr. Henderson!

INT. CLASSROOM - THE NEXT DAY

The classroom is bright and quiet.

Mr. Henderson stands at the board.

MR. HENDERSON
Number one. Navigation.

Zayan sits at his desk. The Nebula-9 action figure stands proudly next to his pencil holder.

Zayan's feet tap. His curls bounce. He snaps his rubber band.

*SNAP.*

He writes "NAVIGATION" on his paper in quick, messy print. He looks at his toy, then at Leo, who gives him a quick thumbs-up from across the aisle.

Zayan smiles. His mind is still racing, and he wouldn't want it any other way.

THE END